# The Next.js app owns /admin, but public/admin/ is still a real directory on
# disk (the legacy .html pages the migration replaced). mod_dir sees that
# directory and 301s /admin -> /admin/, Next then 308s /admin/ back to /admin,
# and the browser gives up on the loop — which took the admin offline.
#
# Turning DirectorySlash off here stops mod_dir adding the slash, so /admin
# reaches the Next route directly. Scoped to this directory so the rest of the
# site's routing is untouched.
DirectorySlash Off

# DirectorySlash Off means a request for this directory is served rather than
# redirected, so listing is disabled explicitly — there is no DirectoryIndex
# here for it to fall back on.
Options -Indexes
